      "writtenOn": "2025-10-02T20:24:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just to make sure I understand this correctly, the `blend_src` members don\u0027t have to be the same as the `location` members? We don\u0027t correlate them here, so that seems to be the case?",
      "revId": "0720fd285c9351abc28361550ad9fed84aa1fcf6",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17cfd98b_76b5e1ab",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/validator.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3173,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000250
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-06T17:08:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If there is any blend_src there must be two members with annotations @location(0) @blend_src(0) and @location(0) @blend_src(1). There maybe other struct members, but they cannot have location annotations explicitly (and implicility blend_src annotations).\n\nCheckBlendSrcAnnotation is responsible for checking location\u003d1 and blend_src\u003d0|1, location_count is just making sure that there are no other location members.\n\nThe language about this is in https://www.w3.org/TR/WGSL/#input-output-locations. It is slightly tricky, because the rule defines \u0027members\u0027 as struct members with location annotations, not just struct members. I had this wrong the first few times I wrote this code...",
      "parentUuid": "dfa0ebca_22ad362b",
